 - **City evacuation — doomed city auto-retreat (land units only)**: in `CvUnitAI::AI_evacuateCity`, the AI now **evacuates 100% of its land units** from a **doomed city**. Previously it often retreated only a tiny fraction (e.g., 2 of 11 defenders vs a 22+ stack, whereas now all 11 defenders would evacuate if the city is deemed doomed). This change might prolong wars/game length (although it is not tested beyond the sample case to know for sure if it would be so), but the intent is a **more competitive, less self-sabotaging** AI. See [KI#62](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#62---extremely-betterstronger-ai-almost-not-evacuating-at-all-doomed-cities-2-swordsmen-in-an-11-unit-defending-stack-vs-a-22-attacking-unit-stack-fixed-by-always-and-100-evacuating-city-doomed-city-regardless-of-land-unit-type-in-cvunitaiai_evacuatecity).
-- **City attack oscillation — pre-check vs strong targets (possible mitigation)**: In `CvUnitAI::AI_attackCityMove`, add a sanity check to **skip marching to/attacking a city** when the **defending stack is too strong**. Goal: prevent the inefficient **advance → abort → backtrack** loop and reduce the risk of being caught without time to retreat. **Note:** in the test sample, this behavior also resolved without the change by running ~2+ autoplay turns in a row instead of 1 turn only from a slightly older save file rather; treat this as a **possible fix/sanity check** (not (at least not yet) broadly tested). See [KI#63](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#63---possibly-prevented-and-possibly-fixed-weird--very-inefficient-back-and-forth-of-going-to-attack-a-city-stack-and-then-going-back-after-seeing-enemy-stack-is-too-strong-i-dont-know-if-this-change-fixes-it-since-the-issue-was-solved-without-it-2-autoplay-turns-were-needed-at-least-it-seems-not-1-but-maybe-this-change-in-cvunitaiai_attackcitymove-helps-a-lot-but-anyways-etc).
-- **Early-game razing — distance-aware captures**: Updated conquer/raze logic so that, for roughly the first **~120 turns** (scaled by game speed), the AI **razes captured cities** that aren’t **close enough** to justify early investment, in `CvPlayerAI::AI_conquerCity`. This addresses the base AdvCiv pattern where forces overextend (most troops sit in a faraway capture while **core cities** thin out) and also preserves scarce early economy (city maintenance, low pop, time to build improvements/culture). Indirect effect: less fog-busting far from us → **more barbarians** there, which tends to pressure rivals. Net: a **stronger, more focused** early AI (fewer “split in two” empires). See [KI#64](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#64---greatly-enhanced-ai-not-razing-faraway-cities-at-captures---now-we-raze-them-if-we-are-in-the-early-game-and-they-are-not-close-enough-thanks-to-changes-and-tweaks-in-cvplayeraiai_conquercity-anyways-etc).
-- **Early defender overbuild → switch to versatile offense (AI)**: Heuristic in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` reduces **early-game overproduction of pure defenders** (especially Longbowmen) by swapping the build to a more **offensive/versatile** unit when defense is already sufficient — e.g., Spearmen, Axemen, Camel Archers, with a preference for civ-specific units like War Chariots when available. Also caps/avoids siege (esp. Trebuchets) when they’re inefficient defensively; production can drop **down to zero** if conditions warrant. If no good replacement exists, the AI can **reflag** the chosen defender to an **attack/attack_city/counter** `UnitAI` instead. In testing, this produced **fewer pure defenders** and **more varied stacks** (e.g., a run where Hatshepsut shifted from ~30 Longbowmen at T130 to ~32 War Chariots, plus Camel Archers). See [KI#53.2](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#532---fixed-and-enhanced-joao-ai-building-way-too-many-defenders-36-longbowmen-at-turn-130-almost-all-with-unitai_city_defense-or-similar-while-being-boxed-in-with-only-3-cities-instead-of-making-about-half-of-these-offense-units-or-versatile-ones-to-punish-overextending-thin-neighbour-fixed-by-having-an-early-phase-we-have-expectedly-too-few-cities-at-this-stage-of-the-game-no-need-to-overbuild-anymore-denders-at-this-stage-of-the-game-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitai-rather-and-our-military-composition-has-way-too-many-defender-unitais-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitais-which-seemingly-fix-the-issue-anyways-etc) and [KI#53.2.2](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#5322-seemingly-greatly-enhanced-ai-overproducing-defenders-early-on-especially-longbowmen-but-not-only-replaced-with-an-early-produce-more-versatile-units-especially-civ-specific-ones-when-defended-enough-at-least-in-theory-anyways-etc-in-cvcityaiai_chooseunit-anyways-etc).
-- **Siege production — conditional minimization (trebuchets especially)**: In `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit`, added targeted checks to keep **siege output** as low as needed—**up to none at all** when conditions say they’re poor value (e.g., when the AI is **weaker** or not preparing **city assaults**). Rationale: **trebuchets** are very **hammer-inefficient** outside direct city attacks; **catapults/cannons** also aren’t versatile enough (and are often misused) for defense. Current tuning intentionally leans **low** versus before (but not permanently zero when other conditions are met). Result: **more varied offensive stacks** and **stronger defense** when behind. See [KI#53.3](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#533-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-siege-units-in-particular-trebuchets-but-not-only-where-they-are-detrimental-to-do-build-in-particular-when-weaker-but-not-only-anyways-etc). **Update:** Thresholds have been **slightly relaxed pre-Renaissance**; **extra-relaxed when holding key strategic bonuses** (**Iron**, **Copper**, **Horse**, **Camel**, **Elephants**) to enable offense windows (e.g., longbow + siege); and **heavily relaxed from Renaissance onward** so **Cannons** can serve as a defensive pivot and the AI avoids over-producing Pikemen into Cuirassiers, and more generally since later sieges units are stronger and more effective, to also have a more varied and effective military composition.
